{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no experiments completed, the highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline and determining whether RNA alone carries sufficient signal. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal, interpretable configuration: a standard linear dimensionality reduction on a single RNA profile with no learned encoder, no aggregation, and no fusion. It serves as the reference floor against which all RNA-encoder choices (scvi, scgpt), profile settings (multiprofile), and multimodal combinations will be compared. Because PCA is computationally cheap, it also uses the experiment budget efficiently, freeing resources for subsequent, more complex runs. If config_001 yields strong accuracy, it confirms RNA is informative and motivates exploring better encoders or multimodal fusion next; if it is weak, it signals that the image modality or learned RNA encoders are critical, redirecting the search. No other single experiment reduces as much downstream uncertainty per unit of compute in the first step."
}

